sional freaky  violence better call Saul season 3 is  worth a watch next up number 8 The  Handmaid's Tale on Hulu now guessing  you've heard of this show before maybe  you've just seen some in the real world  protests with women in red robes from  the show yes it's a super politically  relevant show with some terrifying  parallels to current events I am a  sucker for dystopian future fiction  especially when it stays fiction and  this app tation of Margaret Atwood's  novel about a religious cult that takes  over the government and forces women to  be a slave class for forced breeding is  just so perfectly executed by Elizabeth  moss and the whole team the acting set  designed wardrobe camerawork everything  pulls on some amazing tricks with a  character's limited point of view that  I've never seen a TV show before moving  on to number 7  another darling and my personal book  American vandal on Netflix  true crime documentaries and podcasts  have been all over the place in recent  years and American vandal parodies that  trend so well now if you aren't familiar  it's basically serial or making a  murderer set in a high school with the  mystery being who drew a bunch of dicks  on the teachers cars and of course it  explores this crime with the level of  detail investigative journalism that the  researchers on making a murderer did  which is hilarious but somehow it tricks  you into actually caring about this  mystery and the characters involved  another amazing comedy that  unfortunately can't really devote  resources to cover here is number six on  our list  Nathan for you season four on Comedy  Central now I know on the surface if you  don't watch it the show seems kind of  flat and simple but beneath and Nathan  fielders friendly facade as a business  advise host is a dark uncomfortably  intimate in hilarious cry for help past  guests on his show become running jokes  forming a rich universe of broken toys  the season 4 finale follows the most  fascinating of these weirdos a lonely  Bill Gates impersonator searching the  country for an old flame which totally  overtakes the show's normal format just  trust me just watch a new episodes of  the show you won't be disappointed  moving on to some shows our subscribers  might be more familiar with number 5  Rick and Morty's season 3 on Adult Swim  covering Rick and Morty on this channel  was one of my true delights this year  from the surprise premiere released on  April Fool's Day through pickle rick and  the epic return of evil morty it remains  the best comedy on TV the best sci-fi on  TV and the one show where i genuinely  never have any idea where it's going why  isn't it higher on this list you crazed  Herman head might be screaming at your  screen right now  I don't know while still amazing looking  back a few of the episodes just gonna  slip through the cracks of my memories  somewhere between where I was at 9/11  and my favorite sports bloopers  god I just sound like reddit it's a  great show just go watch my crazy  breakdowns for proof of how much I love  it another show we just couldn't get  around to covering but man you know how  a few years ago everyone was talking  about how true detective was so great  and they were calling it 7 but a TV  series at least that's what I call true  detective but mine honor is truly a  serialized version of 7 it's even got  the same director David Fincher behind  it Fincher is in my opinion the finest  director in the business and he's known  for doing an obsessive number of takes  and that obsession and meticulous  attention to detail weaves its way into  the fabric of the show in the characters  with Jonathan Groff  an FBI agent in the 70s with a fetish  level fascination with serial killers  when the term serial killer was still  being invented the show even kinda  messes with your head - with super  creepy cult opens showing a serial  killer in the making - slow burn but man  is it entertaining  we've been on at number three how could  we leave this off the list Game of  Thrones Season seven on HBO  us watching Game of Thrones is what I  imagine people who care about sports do  when they watch games like I assume the  Patriots have nerd equivalents breaking  down the Shakespeare references right no  that's because we're nuts and season 7  gay fans pretty much everything on our  wish list  Arya killing all the phrasing reuniting  with new mariya check his ami dragon  blowing down the wall check John  revealed as a Targaryen and banging his  aunt Daenerys check yeah I I wanted to  see that I am I got I got issues season  7 wasn't entirely perfect there was the  whole matter of John's and possible  mission north and the relatively  pointless Sansa Arya feud and a weird  amount of poop jokes with Sam at the  Citadel but despite these hiccups Game  of Thrones remains the truly epic  experience that's impossible not to get  wrapped up in 2019 cannot come soon  enough  moving on to number two stranger things  - on Netflix the second season of  stranger things ended up being every bit  the delight of the first season was and  yes the perfectly written and cast kids  were largely to thank but let's be clear  here Bob and Steve Harrington were the  true heroes these two were the step dad  and stepmom that any kid in a tease  dealing with interdimensional D&amp;D  monsters could ask for and ever that  Steve and Dustin would make such a great  power couple but oh man give these two a  spinoff and you feel like crying the  show snuck in the sweetest Easter egg  and he can find out what it was by  watching a breakdown and that brings us  to number one on our list what I  consider to be the best series of 2017  Legion on FX remember what I said about  adapting superheroes well well Legion is  the most creative visually daring and  thoughtful adaptation of a Marvel  character that I have ever seen on  screen on TV or on film showrunner Noah  Holly took a lesser-known figure from  the x-men comics and created